{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1442225-can-you-activate-more-than-one-power-in-a-turn","id":1442225,"title":"Can you activate more than one power in a turn?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-31T20:59:47-07:00","id":1442225,"title":"Can you activate more than one power in a turn?","content":"Like if you want to grow claws and activate a Fortitude power in the same turn, can you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-31T23:55:13-07:00","id":1442229,"title":"","content":"It depends on the powers. There's nothing in the rules that disallows it flatly IIRC, so it comes down to:<br /> <br /> 1) The text of the power (is it reflexive, instant, or described as more involved than that?).<br /> 2) Your PCs ability to pay the costs in one turn (even if you have two Reflexive Disciplines, if they both cost vitae, and you can't spend that much per turn, you can't activate both).<br /> 3) ST interpretations regarding any Disciplines that might logically interfere with each other (more likely in the social Disciplines than physical ones).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T00:06:00-07:00","id":1442230,"title":"","content":"There doesn't seem to be rules for &quot;vitae per turn&quot; anymore, or at least I haven't found the rule if it exists.<br /> <br /> Edit: nevermind, there is a rule at the beginning of the Disciplines section that covers it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-01-2021, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T19:27:29-07:00","id":1444746,"title":"","content":"If you're talking about in v5, no. There is a rule where you can only activate 1 power per turn. It however does say you can also Blood Surge, Blush, and Heal Superficial along with you power, but they all require the usual rouse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}